WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.211
This slide focuses on Nested loops a loop inside a
loop The goal is to

00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:11.844
understand the idea in plain language before
connecting it to code or analytical use Use

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:16.620
carefully A nested loop is useful for grids or
paired combinations but too many layers

00:00:16.647 --> 00:00:22.941
become difficult to read Use nested loops carefully
Before

00:00:22.967 --> 00:00:28.141
running the example predict what the output should
look like Run it in the browser

00:00:28.259 --> 00:00:34.141
inspect the result then change one value condition
or input and run it again Pay

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:39.959
attention to what changed and why The inner loop
finishes for each outer-loop

